Dr. Richter talked about this briefly last week.

431
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:33,800
She may have done it on Saturday, actually.

432
00:29:33,800 --> 00:29:43,240
The cosmology of the ancient world was such that they believed we were surrounded by primordial waters, this great chaos that could crash in on us at any time if God didn't hold it back long.

433
00:29:46,980 --> 00:29:59,480
And we need to hear this in the terms, how many of you have, maybe it's not a show of hands, but you've probably said the ivory tower, she's up in an ivory tower, or he's a knight in shining armor, or that guy's a greedy dragon talking about some billionaire, right?

434
00:29:59,480 --> 00:30:04,220
These are references to things that are not real, but we all immediately know what the imagery means, right?

435
00:30:04,220 --> 00:30:13,720
We don't really think they're knights in shining armor walking around, but it's a shared imagery from our history that allows us to quickly communicate concepts through imagery, through illusion.

436
00:30:14,780 --> 00:30:21,740
But she's in an ivory tower, and it says a tremendous amount about that person from our shared history.

437
00:30:21,740 --> 00:30:28,740
When David, and it's all through Scripture, we sang this morning about you split the sea so I could walk right through it.

438
00:30:28,740 --> 00:30:30,060
That was a real thing that happened.

439
00:30:30,060 --> 00:30:36,880
It was also extra significant to the people of Israel because they believed that showed their God had power over the primordial waters.

440
00:30:37,300 --> 00:30:46,600
It was both a tremendous imagery that he controlled the forces of nature in a way that we don't currently get all the time, as well as a physical salvation.

441
00:30:48,960 --> 00:31:00,380
So when David says, in verse 6, therefore, let everyone who's godly offer prayer at the time when you might be found, surely in the rush of great waters they shall not reach him, he's talking about final judgment.

442
00:31:00,380 --> 00:31:04,720
You'll never hear me say this very often, but in this particular verse, the New Living Translation got it right.

443
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:15,300
So here's how they translated it was, therefore, let the godly pray to you while there is still time, that they may not be drowned in the floodwaters of judgment.

444
00:31:15,300 --> 00:31:16,240
Right?

445
00:31:17,120 --> 00:31:22,200
Does that mean that David actually believes the final judgment will be a flood of waters?

446
00:31:22,200 --> 00:31:22,860
No, it doesn't.

447
00:31:22,860 --> 00:31:24,580
That's the imagery of his people in his time.

448
00:31:24,580 --> 00:31:26,420
But there will be a final cataclysm.

449
00:31:26,420 --> 00:31:28,800
He knows.

450
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:35,540
He may have conceptualized God and sin and last judgment slightly differently from a different perspective than we have.

451
00:31:35,540 --> 00:31:39,480
He had the perspective of a very different culture looking forward from a time before Christ.

452
00:31:40,060 --> 00:31:47,000
But whatever your teleology, your eschatology, your cosmology, your salvation theory, your understanding of atonement, wherever you're coming from,

453
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:51,840
you know that there's a moment when time will stand still for us.

454
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:57,000
And you and I will all come to an unavoidable moment of judgment with God, our maker.

455
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:05,200
A moment when he's going to look us in the face and you'll know that he knows that you know that he knows everything you're pretending is hidden.

456
00:32:05,200 --> 00:32:05,720
Right?

457
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:09,480
You know, he knows everything about you.

458
00:32:09,480 --> 00:32:12,500
Your soul and your history will be laid bare in that moment.

459
00:32:12,500 --> 00:32:15,220
And at that moment, it's too late to say, hey, let's work this out.

